{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 5726696174018345954, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 671, "mtime": 1791872353.5402384, "sha256": "8e9403cd411be20f5455d65b43523ea00cda8f33bd7003052ea47a747d11c1f1"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 373, "mtime": 1791872362.616434, "sha256": "03666b516ddf52b4b6db4b9548596b71512adbad672bb0c516263e9d842404e5"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/27/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/27/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`. Python's built-in `round(x, 2)` works on that stored value, so it rounds down. It also uses banker's rounding at exact halves (ties go to the even digit), not the half-up rounding the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now converts the number to a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`. `repr` gives `\"2.675\"`, the number as it was written, not the stored approximation. The function then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and returns a float, so its signature and return type are the same as before. Halves on negative numbers round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`). `add_vat` uses `round_money`, so it now rounds the same way.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Quick check: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `add_vat(10)\u219212.0`.\n- I added `tests/test_round_money.py` with these cases. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran it and the existing `tests/test_split.py::test_split` directly with `python3`. Both pass.\n\n`add_vat` still multiplies in floats before rounding. If a VAT result lands on an exact half-cent, the multiplication can leave the value just under the half, and it will round down. Fixing that means doing the multiplication in `Decimal` too; I left it alone because it's outside what you asked for.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 277472, "requests_cache_write": 9950, "requests_cost_usd": 0.14865240000000002, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2166, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:t